{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And dwell there, and make there an altar.</b> I do not know what \"and dwell there\" means. It is possible that He commanded him to dwell there first and afterward to make the altar, in order to become purified from idolatry or from the slain that they killed, as in the matter of \"and encamp outside the camp seven days\" (Numbers 31:19), for they had not yet been commanded in the waters of purification, and Jacob hastened in the commandment to become purified before he arrived there. Or \"and let us arise and go up to Bethel\" may be chronologically prior in the narrative, and perhaps He commanded \"and dwell there\" to direct his thought to cleave to El:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:39:39.158362080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}